; GraphEdit's minimap at a NON-default opacity. `minimap_opacity` is the
; minimap's own `modulate.a` (graph_edit.cpp:2786-2791), which multiplies
; every draw inside it — panel, node rect, camera rect, resizer. A regression
; that drops the modulate reads as correct at the default 0.65 in any scene
; that does not move it, because the panel colour alone is plausible.
; Every fixture in this family shares one GraphEdit rect and one GraphNode,
; and `scroll_offset` is deliberately ABSENT from all but
; unit-graph-edit-scroll-offset-clamped.tscn, which exists to move it:
; GraphEdit's own `set_scroll_offset` clamps against min/max bounds that are
; still (0, 0) while a scene's properties are applied (graph_edit.cpp:407), so
; an authored offset moves the grid, the nodes AND the minimap camera at once
; and would mask the one variable each file exists to move.

